WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.211 line:88%
Most portfolios tell you
someone understands security.

00:00:03.251 --> 00:00:04.603 line:88%
This one lets you check.

00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:08.999 line:88%
Meet Alvi Ador: a cybersecurity major
who trains computer-vision models,

00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:11.234 line:88%
and builds the systems that ship them.

00:00:11.625 --> 00:00:15.610 line:88%
Flip the scene from a neural network
into a threat-defense matrix.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.940 line:88%
That panel isn't decoration:
it reads the site's real security posture,

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.221 line:88%
live from the server.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.029 line:88%
Hover the portrait for a face scan.

00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:27.323 line:88%
The background swap runs
on a model in your own browser,

00:00:27.363 --> 00:00:29.558 line:88%
so the photo never leaves your device.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.004 line:88%
The roadmap traces the path: school,
a cybersecurity degree at AIUB,

00:00:35.044 --> 00:00:39.832 line:88%
security labs, a Cisco Ethical Hacker
certificate, and published AI research.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.587 line:88%
Goals are labelled as goals.

00:00:41.627 --> 00:00:43.907 line:88%
Nothing is claimed that isn't earned.

00:00:46.814 --> 00:00:48.204 line:88%
Then it gets hands-on.

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:49.568 line:88%
Write firewall rules,

00:00:49.608 --> 00:00:53.532 line:88%
and real first-match logic decides
which packets get through.

00:00:53.572 --> 00:00:57.235 line:88%
Open SSH to the internet,
and it flags the over-exposure.

00:00:58.463 --> 00:01:02.252 line:88%
Next, the trade-off at the heart
of his emotion-recognition research:

00:01:02.292 --> 00:01:06.357 line:88%
raise the confidence threshold,
and the model stops guessing and abstains.

00:01:06.557 --> 00:01:09.127 line:88%
And this one audits the
very page you're on.

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.440 line:88%
Every security header, graded live: A+.

00:01:12.231 --> 00:01:14.046 line:88%
Research stays in sync on its own,

00:01:14.086 --> 00:01:16.720 line:88%
pulled from the DOI registry
behind ResearchGate,

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.175 line:88%
with a ready-to-use citation
for every paper.

00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:20.747 line:88%
Eight documented builds,

00:01:20.787 --> 00:01:25.159 line:88%
from a zero-knowledge encrypted chat
to a monastery rendered in raw OpenGL,

00:01:25.199 --> 00:01:27.865 line:88%
with live commit history
straight from GitHub.

00:01:28.937 --> 00:01:30.368 line:88%
Credentials are verified,

00:01:30.408 --> 00:01:33.838 line:88%
and kept clearly separate
from what's still in preparation.

00:01:34.804 --> 00:01:38.459 line:88%
The whole interface speaks six
languages, including Bengali,

00:01:38.499 --> 00:01:39.813 line:88%
Alvi's first language.

00:01:40.605 --> 00:01:44.825 line:88%
Power users get a terminal: run a
live security audit, list credentials,

00:01:44.865 --> 00:01:47.309 line:88%
or switch languages from the command line.

00:01:48.098 --> 00:01:51.999 line:88%
When you're ready to talk,
the contact form is hardened end to end:

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:56.705 line:88%
rate-limited, bot-checked, sanitised,
and protected by single-use signed tokens.

00:01:58.405 --> 00:02:02.360 line:88%
Cybersecurity and AI, built
to be checked, not just claimed.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.422 line:88%
Alvi Ador is open to internships
and research collaborations.

